{"id":"15.4.1","doc":"T","title":"Access Configuration","words":379,"blocks":[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":1,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"ESP32-S3's CPU can be configured with different read (R) and write (W) accesses to most of its modules and peripherals independently, from the Secure World and the Non-secure World, by configuring respective registers (PMS_CORE_m_PIF_PMS_CONSTRAN_n_REG)."}]},{"n":2,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Note that permission to modules and peripherals can be configured independently for CPU0 and CPU1 and for the Secure World and Non-secure World."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":3,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Notes on PMS_CORE_m_PIF_PMS_CONSTRAN_n_REG:"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":4,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"m can be 0 or 1 for CPU0 and CPU1 respectively."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":5,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"n can be 1~8, in which 1~4 are for Secure World and 5~8 are for Non-secure World."}]}]}]]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":6,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"For example, users can configure "},{"t":"reg","v":"PMS_CORE_0_PIF_PMS_CONSTRAIN_1_REG"},{"t":"text","v":" [1:0] to 0x2, meaning CPU0 is granted with read access but not write access from the Secure World to "},{"t":"block","v":"UART0","id":"uart"},{"t":"text","v":"."}]},{"n":7,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"In this case, CPU0 won't be able to modify the UART0's internal registers when in Secure World."}]}]},{"t":"table","caption":"Table 15.4-1. Access Configuration of the Peripherals","head":[[{"t":"text","v":"Peripherals"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Secure World"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Non-secure World"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Bit (3)"}]],"rows":[{"n":8,"c":[[{"t":"block","v":"GDMA","id":"gdma"}],[{"t":"reg","v":"PIF_PMS_CONSTRAN_4_REG"}],[{"t":"reg","v":"PIF_PMS_CONSTRAN_8_REG"}],[{"t":"text","v":"[7:6]"}]]},{"n":9,"c":[[{"t":"block","v":"eFuse","id":"efuse"},{"t":"text","v":" Controller & PMU (2)"}],[{"t":"reg","v":"PIF_PMS_CONSTRAN_1_REG"}],[{"t":"reg","v":"PIF_PMS_CONSTRAN_5_REG"}],[{"t":"text","v":"[15:14]"}]]},{"n":10,"c":[[{"t":"tex